ed by this exact spelling; multiple persons under one unchanged source article remain together. Actual proper-name capitalization and whole-name boundaries required. Explicit occurrence-level ambiguity exclusions override this rule.","sourceHeadwordId":"Jacob","term":"Jacob"}],"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","matchingRules":["reviewed_exact_headword"],"sourceProvenanceId":"Jacob","sourceTitle":"Jacob"},{"evidence":[{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[{"anchorIndex":1,"href":"?bref=Ps.24.1-2","rawReference":"Ps.24.1-2"}],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"A Psalm of David. The earth is the LORD’s, and the fullness thereof, the world and all who dwell therein.","verse":1},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"Who may ascend the hill of the LORD? Who may stand in His holy place?","verse":3},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"He will receive blessing from the LORD and vindication from the God of his salvation.","verse":5},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"Who is this King of Glory? The LORD strong and mighty, the LORD mighty in battle.","verse":8},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"Who is He, this King of Glory? The LORD of Hosts—He is the King of Glory. Selah","verse":10}],"id":"Lord","label":"LORD","matchReviews":[{"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","scope":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","senseReview":"Only literal uppercase LORD is admitted globally. Source Lord article explicitly covers God as Lord; lowercase human lord and sentence-title Lord are not inferred from this rule.","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord","term":"LORD"}],"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","matchingRules":["reviewed_exact_headword"],"sourceProvenanceId":"Lord","sourceTitle":"Lord"}],"format":"bsb-study-chapter-v2","notes":[{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":["God’s Presence in the Psalms"],"sourceClass":"theme-title","t":"h"},{"c":["Scripture writers often express the desire to experience God’s presence. In the intimate experience of his presence, God’s rich goodness and love are all that people need (see ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.21.6","r":"Ps.21.6","rawR":"Ps.21.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.21.6","value":"Ps.21.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 21:6"},"). By the same token, the absence of God’s presence is distressing and damaging."],"sourceClass":"theme-body-fl","t":"p"},{"c":["The poets of Israel often spoke of God’s face as a way of expressing his presence or absence. So they sought his face (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.24.6","r":"Ps.24.6","rawR":"Ps.24.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.24.6","value":"Ps.24.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"24:6"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.105.4","r":"Ps.105.4","rawR":"Ps.105.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.105.4","value":"Ps.105.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"105:4"},"). When his face shone or was turned toward his people, they experienced his presence in blessing, provision, and protection (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.67.1","r":"Ps.67.1","rawR":"Ps.67.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.67.1","value":"Ps.67.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"67:1"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.80.3-19","r":"Ps.80.3-19","rawR":"Ps.80.3-19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.80.3-19","value":"Ps.80.3-19"}],"t":"ref","v":"80:3-19"},"). God’s hiding his face from his people was a picture of divine abandonment (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.13.1","r":"Ps.13.1","rawR":"Ps.13.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.13.1","value":"Ps.13.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"13:1"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.27.9","r":"Ps.27.9","rawR":"Ps.27.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.27.9","value":"Ps.27.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"27:9"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.44.24","r":"Ps.44.24","rawR":"Ps.44.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.44.24","value":"Ps.44.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"44:24"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.69.17","r":"Ps.69.17","rawR":"Ps.69.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.69.17","value":"Ps.69.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"69:17"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.88.14","r":"Ps.88.14","rawR":"Ps.88.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.88.14","value":"Ps.88.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"88:14"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.89.46","r":"Ps.89.46","rawR":"Ps.89.46","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.89.46","value":"Ps.89.46"}],"t":"ref","v":"89:46"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.102.2","r":"Ps.102.2","rawR":"Ps.102.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.102.2","value":"Ps.102.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"102:2"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.104.29","r":"Ps.104.29","rawR":"Ps.104.29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.104.29","value":"Ps.104.29"}],"t":"ref","v":"104:29"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.143.7","r":"Ps.143.7","rawR":"Ps.143.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.143.7","value":"Ps.143.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"143:7"},"), as if God were not seeing or hearing them (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.10.11","r":"Ps.10.11","rawR":"Ps.10.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.10.11","value":"Ps.10.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"10:11"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.42.3","r":"Ps.42.3","rawR":"Ps.42.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.42.3","value":"Ps.42.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"42:3"},"). The absence of God creates dismay, shame, and chaos, and may even lead to death (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.30.7","r":"Ps.30.7","rawR":"Ps.30.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.30.7","value":"Ps.30.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"30:7"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.44.24","r":"Ps.44.24","rawR":"Ps.44.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.44.24","value":"Ps.44.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"44:24"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.104.29","r":"Ps.104.29","rawR":"Ps.104.29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.104.29","value":"Ps.104.29"}],"t":"ref","v":"104:29"},")."],"sourceClass":"theme-body","t":"p"},{"c":["The psalmists prayed for God’s presence as they requested a change in their circumstances (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.31.15-16","r":"Ps.31.15-16","rawR":"Ps.31.15-16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.31.15-16","value":"Ps.31.15-16"}],"t":"ref","v":"31:15-16"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.67.1","r":"Ps.67.1","rawR":"Ps.67.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.67.1","value":"Ps.67.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"67:1"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.69.17","r":"Ps.69.17","rawR":"Ps.69.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.69.17","value":"Ps.69.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"69:17"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.80.3","r":"Ps.80.3","rawR":"Ps.80.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.80.3","value":"Ps.80.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"80:3"},", ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.80.7","r":"Ps.80.7","rawR":"Ps.80.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.80.7","value":"Ps.80.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"7"},", ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.80.19","r":"Ps.80.19","rawR":"Ps.80.19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.80.19","value":"Ps.80.19"}],"t":"ref","v":"19"},"), and they acknowledged the role of his presence in giving them aid (see ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.44.3","r":"Ps.44.3","rawR":"Ps.44.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.44.3","value":"Ps.44.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"44:3"},"). The godly long to be invited into God’s presence (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.11.7","r":"Ps.11.7","rawR":"Ps.11.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.11.7","value":"Ps.11.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"11:7"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.16.9-11","r":"Ps.16.9-11","rawR":"Ps.16.9-11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.16.9-11","value":"Ps.16.9-11"}],"t":"ref","v":"16:9-11"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.17.15","r":"Ps.17.15","rawR":"Ps.17.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.17.15","value":"Ps.17.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"17:15"},"). His presence alone satisfies their deepest longing (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.17.15","r":"Ps.17.15","rawR":"Ps.17.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.17.15","value":"Ps.17.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"17:15"},") and gives them lasting pleasure (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.37.4","r":"Ps.37.4","rawR":"Ps.37.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.37.4","value":"Ps.37.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"37:4"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.43.4","r":"Ps.43.4","rawR":"Ps.43.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.43.4","value":"Ps.43.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"43:4"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.73.25","r":"Ps.73.25","rawR":"Ps.73.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.73.25","value":"Ps.73.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"73:25"},"). Everything about God delights them."],"sourceClass":"theme-body","t":"p"},{"c":["God’s favor and goodness are realized in his presence (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.23.6","r":"Ps.23.6","rawR":"Ps.23.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.23.6","value":"Ps.23.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"23:6"},"), as demonstrated in his people’s experiences of blessing, abundant crops, and prosperity (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.21.3","r":"Ps.21.3","rawR":"Ps.21.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.21.3","value":"Ps.21.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"21:3"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.65.11","r":"Ps.65.11","rawR":"Ps.65.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.65.11","value":"Ps.65.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"65:11"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.68.10","r":"Ps.68.10","rawR":"Ps.68.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.68.10","value":"Ps.68.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"68:10"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.85.12","r":"Ps.85.12","rawR":"Ps.85.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.85.12","value":"Ps.85.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"85:12"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.106.5","r":"Ps.106.5","rawR":"Ps.106.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.106.5","value":"Ps.106.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"106:5"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.128.2","r":"Ps.128.2","rawR":"Ps.128.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.128.2","value":"Ps.128.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"128:2"},"). Thus God’s goodness and the Temple—the place where his presence is especially manifest—are closely linked (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.65.4","r":"Ps.65.4","rawR":"Ps.65.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.65.4","value":"Ps.65.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"65:4"},"). God’s presence leads to health and vitality among his people, and he satisfies his people who are in need (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.107.9","r":"Ps.107.9","rawR":"Ps.107.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.107.9","value":"Ps.107.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"107:9"},"). For the psalmists, God’s presence was essential for flourishing."],"sourceClass":"theme-body","t":"p"},{"c":["Passages for Further Study"],"sourceClass":"theme-refs-title","t":"h"},{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.4.6","r":"Ps.4.6","rawR":"Ps.4.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.4.6","value":"Ps.4.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Pss 4:6"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.13.1","r":"Ps.13.1","rawR":"Ps.13.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.13.1","value":"Ps.13.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"13:1"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.21.6","r":"Ps.21.6","rawR":"Ps.21.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.21.6","value":"Ps.21.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"21:6"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.24.3-6","r":"Ps.24.3-6","rawR":"Ps.24.3-6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.24.3-6","value":"Ps.24.3-6"}],"t":"ref","v":"24:3-6"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.27.9","r":"Ps.27.9","rawR":"Ps.27.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.27.9","value":"Ps.27.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"27:9"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.44.3","r":"Ps.44.3","rawR":"Ps.44.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.44.3","value":"Ps.44.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"44:3"},", ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.44.24","r":"Ps.44.24","rawR":"Ps.44.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.44.24","value":"Ps.44.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"24"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.67.1","r":"Ps.67.1","rawR":"Ps.67.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.67.1","value":"Ps.67.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"67:1"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.69.17","r":"Ps.69.17","rawR":"Ps.69.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.69.17","value":"Ps.69.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"69:17"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.88.14","r":"Ps.88.14","rawR":"Ps.88.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.88.14","value":"Ps.88.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"88:14"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.89.46","r":"Ps.89.46","rawR":"Ps.89.46","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.89.46","value":"Ps.89.46"}],"t":"ref","v":"89:46"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.102.2","r":"Ps.102.2","rawR":"Ps.102.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.102.2","value":"Ps.102.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"102:2"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.104.29","r":"Ps.104.29","rawR":"Ps.104.29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.104.29","value":"Ps.104.29"}],"t":"ref","v":"104:29"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.143.7","r":"Ps.143.7","rawR":"Ps.143.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.143.7","value":"Ps.143.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"143:7"}],"sourceClass":"theme-refs","t":"p"}],"id":"ThemeNote:GodsPresenceinthePsalms","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":24,"endVerse":6,"startChapter":24,"startVerse":3}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"GodsPresenceinthePsalms","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"ThemeNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[24],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"ad801074575cf3bee3cc0f742243cf912091ad4df2ee3627a7570d6f7d5ce718","sourceItemName":"GodsPresenceinthePsalms","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/ThemeNotes.xml","sourceOrder":112,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.24.3-6","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":"God’s Presence in the Psalms","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"God’s Presence in the Psalms","type":"ThemeNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.20.1-24.10","r":"Ps.20.1-24.10","rawR":"Ps.20.1-24.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.20.1-24.10","value":"Ps.20.1-24.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Pss 20–24"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," This sequence of psalms expresses the experience of moving from confidence and commitment (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.20.1-21.13","r":"Ps.20.1-21.13","rawR":"Ps.20.1-21.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.20.1-21.13","value":"Ps.20.1-21.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Pss 20–21"},"), through anguish and abandonment (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.22.1-31","r":"Ps.22.1-31","rawR":"Ps.22.1-31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.22.1-31","value":"Ps.22.1-31"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 22"},"), and finally to comfort, insight, and hope (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.23.1-24.10","r":"Ps.23.1-24.10","rawR":"Ps.23.1-24.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.23.1-24.10","value":"Ps.23.1-24.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Pss 23–24"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.20.1-24.10","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":24,"endVerse":10,"startChapter":20,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.20.1-24.10","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[20,21,22,23,24],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"5df1d0f4875f3ea1d1c2cf769acf98707968ff9dc4eb2fb1123634b85c59c7a6","sourceItemName":"Ps.20.1-24.10","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":6158,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.20.1-24.10","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.20.1-24.10","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.23.1-28.9","r":"Ps.23.1-28.9","rawR":"Ps.23.1-28.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.23.1-28.9","value":"Ps.23.1-28.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"Pss 23–28"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," These psalms develop the importance of integrity (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.25.4-7","r":"Ps.25.4-7","rawR":"Ps.25.4-7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.25.4-7","value":"Ps.25.4-7"}],"t":"ref","v":"25:4-7"},", ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.25.12-14","r":"Ps.25.12-14","rawR":"Ps.25.12-14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.25.12-14","value":"Ps.25.12-14"}],"t":"ref","v":"12-14"},", ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.25.21","r":"Ps.25.21","rawR":"Ps.25.21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.25.21","value":"Ps.25.21"}],"t":"ref","v":"21"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.26.6","r":"Ps.26.6","rawR":"Ps.26.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.26.6","value":"Ps.26.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"26:6"},", ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.26.11","r":"Ps.26.11","rawR":"Ps.26.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.26.11","value":"Ps.26.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"11"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.27.7-12","r":"Ps.27.7-12","rawR":"Ps.27.7-12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.27.7-12","value":"Ps.27.7-12"}],"t":"ref","v":"27:7-12"},"), God’s shepherding care (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.23.1","r":"Ps.23.1","rawR":"Ps.23.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.23.1","value":"Ps.23.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"23:1"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.28.9","r":"Ps.28.9","rawR":"Ps.28.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.28.9","value":"Ps.28.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"28:9"},"), God’s guidance (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.23.2-3","r":"Ps.23.2-3","rawR":"Ps.23.2-3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.23.2-3","value":"Ps.23.2-3"}],"t":"ref","v":"23:2-3"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.25.5","r":"Ps.25.5","rawR":"Ps.25.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.25.5","value":"Ps.25.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"25:5"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.27.11","r":"Ps.27.11","rawR":"Ps.27.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.27.11","value":"Ps.27.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"27:11"},"), God’s goodness (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.23.6","r":"Ps.23.6","rawR":"Ps.23.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.23.6","value":"Ps.23.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"23:6"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.25.7-8","r":"Ps.25.7-8","rawR":"Ps.25.7-8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.25.7-8","value":"Ps.25.7-8"}],"t":"ref","v":"25:7-8"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.27.13","r":"Ps.27.13","rawR":"Ps.27.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.27.13","value":"Ps.27.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"27:13"},"), and living in his house (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.23.6","r":"Ps.23.6","rawR":"Ps.23.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.23.6","value":"Ps.23.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"23:6"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.26.8","r":"Ps.26.8","rawR":"Ps.26.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.26.8","value":"Ps.26.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"26:8"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.27.4","r":"Ps.27.4","rawR":"Ps.27.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.27.4","value":"Ps.27.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"27:4"},", ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.27.8","r":"Ps.27.8","rawR":"Ps.27.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.27.8","value":"Ps.27.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"8"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.23.1-28.9","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":28,"endVerse":9,"startChapter":23,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.23.1-28.9","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[23,24,25,26,27,28],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"3d421a5bd98a2c78ba9a5046fb3b46dfd76fdde16fe27ca0acb4bdfa4aaec79b","sourceItemName":"Ps.23.1-28.9","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":6207,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.23.1-28.9","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.23.1-28.9","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.24.1-10","r":"Ps.24.1-10","rawR":"Ps.24.1-10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.24.1-10","value":"Ps.24.1-10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 24"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The shepherd of ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.23.1-6","r":"Ps.23.1-6","rawR":"Ps.23.1-6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.23.1-6","value":"Ps.23.1-6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 23"},", who is also the King of the whole world, takes possession of Zion."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.24.1-10","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":24,"endVerse":10,"startChapter":24,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.24.1-10","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[24],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"ae4e4f216bad02d350814c8818680f3ec80a4d6a308a900cdd2d1296faed88cc","sourceItemName":"Ps.24.1-10","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":6216,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceSta